{"title":"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2:_Scaling_and_combining_triangles\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2: Scaling and combining triangles</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3:_Trial_and_Error\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3: Trial and Error</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4:\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4:</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5:_Ptolemy_(no_trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5: Ptolemy (no trig)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6(rough_value)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6(rough value)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Angle_Addition)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Angle Addition)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Geometry_Solution_Without_Words)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Geometry Solution Without Words)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9_(Complex_Number)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9 (Complex Number)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_10_(Double_Angle_+_Co-function_Identity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 10 (Double Angle + Co-function Identity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Solution_11_(don&#39;t_do_this)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 11 (don't do this)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Solution_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(🚀_2_min_solve_🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (🚀 2 min solve 🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_-_MaffyTaffy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution - MaffyTaffy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the radian measure of the smallest angle in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351938ecd2dcd45f7415d5062d32fedc601011f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3{-}4{-}5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" /> right triangle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> be the radian measure of the smallest angle in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/8/df8ce93516dc68f34fba7e4dc307bc76e5172f8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7{-}24{-}25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> right triangle. In terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef43715351652041d84a70bf86dd004f0d123493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{\\alpha}{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\alpha - \\frac{\\pi}{8}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{\\pi}{2} - 2\\alpha \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\pi - 4\\alpha\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"535\" height=\"34\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/413c1ed8a92e0575b8cf656affc8a33db73786a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan\\alpha=\\frac{3}{4} \\text{ and } \\tan\\beta=\\frac{7}{24}.\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"38\" />\nWe have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/0/e20adae2dd89a269ba4730d96730cead3b680bbd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\tan(\\alpha+\\beta) &amp;= \\frac{\\tan\\alpha+\\tan\\beta}{1-\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{7}{24}}{1-\\frac{3}{4} \\cdot \\frac{7}{24}} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{4}{3}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"228\" height=\"138\" />\nIt follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb63accabcaede55b863f8c92f4a5043d94fb12d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\alpha+\\beta&amp;=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right) \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right) \\\\ &amp;=\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\alpha. \\end{align*}\" width=\"189\" height=\"131\" />\nTherefore, the answer is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc60484669f3ff5f4f4e24226ee68839f6722558.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\beta=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{\\pi}{2}-2\\alpha}.\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"44\" />\n~lptoggled\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2:_Scaling_and_combining_triangles\">Solution 2: Scaling and combining triangles</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2: Scaling and combining triangles\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can scale the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangle up by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to make its side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e303870d8a0aff8385662c155e8f813f0a62bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18,24,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/f/72f1e19ce0046fe93153f4a699dbe21d86fe9b30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> then glue its side of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to the corresponding side in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangle:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/1/45133802d0df1d0ddfd0328d39295a86f8f96f2c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A = (0,0); pair B = (18,0); pair C = (25,0); pair D = (18,24);  draw(A--C--D--cycle); draw(B--D);  draw(rightanglemark(C,B,D,50));  label(&quot;A&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;B&quot;, B, S); label(&quot;C&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;D&quot;, D, N);  label(&quot;18&quot;, A--B, S); label(&quot;7&quot;, B--C, S); label(&quot;25&quot;, C--D, NE); label(&quot;30&quot;, D--A, NW); label(&quot;24&quot;, B--D, W);  label(&quot;$\\alpha$&quot;, D, 6*dir(250)); label(&quot;$\\beta$&quot;, D, 9*dir(278)); label(&quot;$\\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\alpha$&quot;, A, 4*dir(25)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"245\" />\n</p><p>Angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1fc15d59287d2ff7bf581a84f348b3207a0c64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/62778c987facd63dd959286c9d4ab82d6b641c25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDA$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> are complementary in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3a6c9fd0a76228e2ac0017f40e2422dd517092b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc8c384390fc0109be488f4615ab59dd0053e37d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAB = \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\alpha.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"34\" /> We also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40237fd1fe94d892cafe96ff855f278bb1451b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 18 + 7 = 25 = CD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles. That means that its base angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/2/f52ad9ae2045af1a306a7815747c10c997abc4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDA$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f105551f628f107282e0cc6c89063f3c1faece9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAD$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> are congruent, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/e/1fe89f1a9475817eacd9bf3d00f428ab548d23f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta = \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\alpha,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"125\" height=\"34\" /> and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be171b0df0fae57f670a8feb44d280283d238d96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{\\pi}{2}-2\\alpha}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"147\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>~MartianTom\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3:_Trial_and_Error\">Solution 3: Trial and Error</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3: Trial and Error\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Another approach to solving this problem is trial and error, comparing the sine of the answer choices with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e0dd01c691469a3faa9aafa1297f0de5e79d9d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\beta = \\frac{7}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"38\" />. Starting with the easiest sine to compute from the answer choices (option choice D). We get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc7984f54d767f0b8a190e79582084f4af0de0c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1 - \\cos{\\alpha}}{2}}\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/6285d4f10dd2b2d463b07b6b5b31142e129017d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\sqrt{\\frac{1 - \\frac{4}{5}}{2}}\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a89c614d76def405701996466ba610d43b74c45.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{10}}\\]\" width=\"58\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4c6a0bdf975759c073a6e0cdab4bf4944591d7b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\neq \\frac{7}{25}\\]\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The next easiest sine to compute is option choice C.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/7447cc393f3c5e1492fa92792f98bb289530a746.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - 2\\alpha\\right)} = \\sin{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(2\\alpha\\right)}\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"33\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63bb2aee4d27bd6bd2800b96aa09be1e4721e090.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\cos{2\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748231d1fb7f1cc4112820b455a9e8aa5535997f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\cos^2{\\alpha} - \\sin^2{\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/6/e6674d0d8845bb7495ae28e8efb94fd895e7c16f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\frac{16}{25} - \\frac{9}{25}\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/6/086d6daa24bb018a7d19505a1a5daacf9f7080c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\frac{7}{25}\\]\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23d492e1a0a304e5967ff1ad79b05e6bf9d3fd10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - 2\\alpha\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"35\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a837f4c18176bac355d37d2a238f05674055dcd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, option choice C is the correct answer. ~amshah\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4:\">Solution 4:</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4:\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/4/4a45ac828bc4c3b5a5af6998edd864fcdbfd3e88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(B) = \\frac{24}{25} = 2 \\cdot \\frac{12}{25} = 2 \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\cdot \\frac{4}{5}  = 2 \\cdot \\sin(A) \\cdot \\cos(A) = \\sin(2A)  = \\cos(90^{\\circ} - 2A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"633\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40a0ee871c23fee2f00797d7ea8a819b4c2ccb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\beta=\\boxed{(C) \\frac{\\pi}{2} -2\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p><p>Added Note: It should be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/8/af8f9c94bda017423ef4ce21b1470e281c24ae04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(B) = \\frac{24}{25} = 2 \\cdot \\frac{12}{25} = 2 \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\cdot \\frac{4}{5}  = 2 \\cdot \\sin(A) \\cdot \\cos(A) = \\sin(2A)  = \\cos(90^{\\circ} - 2A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"635\" height=\"38\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204757541e20d28b6637d16b40ace282f2f621af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"20\" /> is actually <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a09bb4f263378b16ce902682c0364edc2556f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />!\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Hello_2d_world&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Hello 2d world (page does not exist)\">Hello 2d world</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User_talk:Hello_2d_world&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User talk:Hello 2d world (page does not exist)\">talk</a>) 08:45, 22 August 2025 (EDT)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5:_Ptolemy_.28no_trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5:_Ptolemy_(no_trig)\">Solution 5: Ptolemy (no trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5: Ptolemy (no trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let AB have length 15, BC have length 20, AC length 25, AD length 7 and CD length 24. Let x be the measure of segment BD. Thus the measure of angle ACB is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and the measure of angle ACD is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />. ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral because angle ABC and angle ADC are right angles. Using Ptolemy's theorem on this quadrilateral yields 25x = 15*24 + 7*20 = 500, or x = 20. This means triangle CBD is isoceles. The perpendicular bisector of CD passes through the center (O) of the circle on which ABCD lies and also passes through B. Let the intersection of the perpendicular bisector of CD and CD be point P. The measure of angle OBC is the same as the measure of the angle OCB which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, so the measure of angle BOC is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b55d34fb4a5a596a558d40aa1ba7595f6d4e873.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\pi} - {2}{\\alpha}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />, so the measure of angle COP is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70486e3698e56d8864bcceb1dfa53307446bafd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${2}{\\alpha}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" />. Triangle COP is a right triangle with angle OCP being the same as angle ACD (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />), angle COP being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70486e3698e56d8864bcceb1dfa53307446bafd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${2}{\\alpha}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" />, and angle CPO being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aeebb746f8c0d3dac5219c3635617032430afee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" />. \nSo: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c802abbc605c15f75e713c923200477098527f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\beta + {2}\\alpha + \\frac{\\pi}{2} = \\pi\\]\" width=\"126\" height=\"32\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40a0ee871c23fee2f00797d7ea8a819b4c2ccb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\beta=\\boxed{(C) \\frac{\\pi}{2} -2\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"44\" />~Ilaggo2432\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6.28rough_value.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6(rough_value)\">Solution 6(rough value)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6(rough value)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>given in the question,sin(a)is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daadf8d12321aa8913af98e9ccb98f4ddfd9616c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> and sin (b) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/34036a68d00c6ecbbd880ae59d77813c6be0e972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7/25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" />, estimate the angle by using the arcsin function. arcsin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daadf8d12321aa8913af98e9ccb98f4ddfd9616c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> is around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/a/97acc7a1c4c56b780bc42222a75e36cdc9cdb378.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.643$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> rad and arcsin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/34036a68d00c6ecbbd880ae59d77813c6be0e972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7/25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> is around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f7bed8fc3195dad01d796a25aa959b8b359cdc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.283.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/039bf945c704ff98e6f81626bbad32550cc37193.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> is closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c40baa67136b0c1e96aa2f316f259a5707b7eb4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.57$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> rad, try one by one and option c suggests that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb53fafb1cf77219a29ce2d2188053fba2c9b5f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1.57=2(0.643)+0.283.\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" /> My first amc 12 edit\nmine too\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Angle_Addition.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Angle_Addition)\">Solution 7 (Angle Addition)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Angle Addition)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c4531b80e6d97cd72788d1fe6b117d3618b9ae85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\beta)\\cos(\\alpha) = \\sin(\\alpha+\\beta) = \\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"369\" height=\"38\" />. Noticing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe2ea2b836b2c9be0281b856ac80a8e0e3002364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{5} = \\cos(\\alpha) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\alpha\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"209\" height=\"38\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/224cc0a580f0443a53d621ac27f29987c0233b52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta = \\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"120\" height=\"34\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/7/b37d85ebd00e0ba7cb86a345c8363e4a606a2501.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} - 2\\alpha}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"106\" height=\"46\" />\n~KEVIN_LIU\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Geometry_Solution_Without_Words.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Geometry_Solution_Without_Words)\">Solution 8 (Geometry Solution Without Words)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Geometry Solution Without Words)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/86622a5c1aa47d67be36528fdfc00b1814dca2c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle A+ \\angle B+ \\angle A = \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"32\" /> \nTherefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40a0ee871c23fee2f00797d7ea8a819b4c2ccb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\beta=\\boxed{(C) \\frac{\\pi}{2} -2\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"44\" />\n~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2024_amc12A_p10.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/47/2024_amc12A_p10.PNG/400px-2024_amc12A_p10.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"391\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/47/2024_amc12A_p10.PNG/600px-2024_amc12A_p10.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/47/2024_amc12A_p10.PNG 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_9_.28Complex_Number.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9_(Complex_Number)\">Solution 9 (Complex Number)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9 (Complex Number)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83a9385d5f629ad66386240a581d8db4cbeb9a4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_{A} = 4 + 3i = 5e^{iA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fea94475acc7bae64a1868168791ae55097adb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_{B} = 24 + 7i = 25e^{iB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Looking at the answer choices, we start by testing out an easier choice, such as C.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/5/95553bc056ec44ae8aee2d62c5b14e03d66362fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4+3i)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2b247a266a283fe829da5dccc551647fe823e9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 16 + 9 \\cdot i^2 + 2\\cdot12 \\cdot i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00b65a7d8866ed17568a8d11365ebe8812feee8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 16 - 9 + 24i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5b399aa2e3b75c24b4f21c6469ed11a3f52d1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 7 + 24i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Finally:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/c/c4c7e35711b3f076dc449809f1f306cb69ee36bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25^2 \\cdot e^{i(2A+B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24da796bd261613e15ed79f4d540c68f2404fa20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 25e^{i2A} \\cdot 25e^{iB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/5/60508092c0821239378188f44056e58323999f4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$={(5e^{iA})}^2 \\cdot 25e^{iB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd0f1425764ee146b45e07c9e232bceb7bc454f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= (7+24i)(24+7i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/8865bdf050a09e7c4820f1f513f9a4149da34873.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=25^2i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8a85f4799a28bb35fcd509e59412ef5476fe24b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=25^2 e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>This proves that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/3/5a3f54eb13a7290217150f05fab3c2cefc646b23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle 2A+ \\angle B = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"126\" height=\"34\" />. (Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3d83803f2489e0c9f39769acd91515d78783ce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A &lt; \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/21347c45008d9c17e54f1e89b8f87fd4bd9caec3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B &lt; \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"34\" />)\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40a0ee871c23fee2f00797d7ea8a819b4c2ccb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\beta=\\boxed{(C) \\frac{\\pi}{2} -2\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_10_.28Double_Angle_.2B_Co-function_Identity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_10_(Double_Angle_+_Co-function_Identity)\">Solution 10 (Double Angle + Co-function Identity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 10 (Double Angle + Co-function Identity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e8725b758dd4b1375b3a1097a78e776c98ae516.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(\\alpha) = \\frac{4}{5} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\sin(\\alpha) = \\frac{3}{5}\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Use a double angle identity to calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f09d0531a38886b78bd09abf8ee41d8bbdedc7e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(2\\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d4aacbd6a1253b9b47163786b48af6bb5fec711.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(2\\alpha) = \\cos^2(\\alpha) - \\sin^2(\\alpha) = \\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^2 - \\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^2 = \\frac{16}{25} - \\frac{9}{25} = \\frac{7}{25}\\]\" width=\"494\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>We know that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744026bd154b7086da8e6279228785d76020a752.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\beta) = \\frac{7}{25}\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Equate both to each other:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/9488e2d2ab893c38aa953dd7018991636a868d7b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(2\\alpha) = \\sin(\\beta)\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Apply the co-function identity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff60b18de94821e359332d521288bf0ed13912e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(2\\alpha) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - 2\\alpha\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"190\" height=\"35\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16d1d0f02de37b82ce94e4c0add7077bd1f82b48.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - 2\\alpha\\right) = \\sin(\\beta)\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>Hence,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a296696745534fac0b409ce426131c99ddc92194.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\beta=\\boxed{(\\mathbf{C}) \\frac{\\pi}{2} - 2\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>~sourodeepdeb\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_11_.28don.27t_do_this.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_11_(don't_do_this)\">Solution 11 (don't do this)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 11 (don&#39;t do this)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036f921005632531ad6772b9905bc9c1f011eebc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{5} \\approx \\alpha-\\frac{\\alpha^{3}}{6}\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd530052f20fc31ecdf94f0bf821d015f9056b4d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-5\\alpha^3+30\\alpha-18 \\approx 0\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa1ee6c3ce7cd1a0691614c15a825527ee8b0c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\alpha \\approx 0.64464\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73ecb3a4ec51785ce6f0ecb1cda579f462a4792c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{7}{25} \\approx \\beta-\\frac{\\beta^{3}}{6}\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ff956c9bd2e13ef18ee0074d3c159c6d47e35d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-25\\beta^3+150\\beta-42 \\approx 0\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/337f5cd39a6e19d212323bb7b928a5ae5f552968.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\beta \\approx 0.28381\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f77334b80d48b696a2dd3d04577d9a5258b3b339.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\pi}{2} - 2 \\cdot 0.64464 \\approx 0.28151632679 \\approx \\beta\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a296696745534fac0b409ce426131c99ddc92194.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\beta=\\boxed{(\\mathbf{C}) \\frac{\\pi}{2} - 2\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_12\">Solution 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/7/307760b83acf2d5cff6b8bf3a7026315c5f56f37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4}{5} \\approx 1-\\frac{\\alpha^2}{2}\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa078a2e1668d2e2f006053ffc0a7d775535b098.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5\\alpha^2 \\approx 2\\]\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/199eab8e40b2da01b29af3ce6cd2494399794a3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\alpha \\approx \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{5}} \\approx 0.63246\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/4149c034e4905e4e1703f0bbef4b65d96de3ad6d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{24}{25} \\approx 1-\\frac{\\beta^2}{2}\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/1/9e10e7afd741032a6d59569e606b956700007b3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[25\\beta^2 \\approx 2\\]\" width=\"69\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6804f5acb59c1db28a20b0cdad2d875c48f3791.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\beta \\approx \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{25}} \\approx 0.28284\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12e73977f5dc0b5d3cf95f22c14569ee682af1e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\pi}{2} - 2 \\cdot 0.63246 \\approx 0.30587632679  \\approx \\beta\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a296696745534fac0b409ce426131c99ddc92194.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\beta=\\boxed{(\\mathbf{C}) \\frac{\\pi}{2} - 2\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28.F0.9F.9A.80_2_min_solve_.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(🚀_2_min_solve_🚀)\">Video Solution (🚀 2 min solve 🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-e